response:
The report describes a fraudulent scheme targeting Ukrainian citizens to steal payment card data. Threat actors set up a Facebook page named "UA Blog" to promote fake surveys promising cash rewards. The ads redirect victims through several domains (airmauritiusticket.com, gangbang6.monster, great-surveys.top) and finally to a phishing form on accept-pay.top, which captures payment card credentials. Infrastructure used in the scheme includes IP addresses located in Russia and Germany, and services behind CloudFlare.

